# paw 🐾

A small, accessible React component library with just enough style to get you started.

**paw** provides 12 composable UI primitives, sensible defaults, TypeScript types, and no runtime CSS-in-JS dependency. Use the included stylesheet, override it with CSS variables, or bring your own styles.

## Features

- 12 focused UI primitives
- Accessible keyboard and focus behavior
- Controlled and uncontrolled APIs where appropriate
- TypeScript support and forwarded refs
- Lightweight, themeable CSS
- Works with React 18+ and React 19

## Installation

```sh
npm install paw
```

```sh
pnpm add paw
```

```sh
yarn add paw
```

React and React DOM are peer dependencies:

```sh
npm install react react-dom
```

## Quick start

Import the optional base stylesheet once, near the root of your application:

```tsx
import "paw/styles.css";
```

Then use the primitives like regular React components:

```tsx
import { useState } from "react";
import { Badge, Button, Card, Input } from "paw";

export function ProfileForm() {
  const [name, setName] = useState("");

  return (
    <Card>
      <Badge variant="success">Active</Badge>

      <label htmlFor="profile-name">Display name</label>
      <Input
        id="profile-name"
        value={name}
        onChange={(event) => setName(event.target.value)}
        placeholder="Ada Lovelace"
      />

      <Button disabled={!name.trim()} onClick={() => alert(`Saved ${name}`)}>
        Save profile
      </Button>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

## Components

| Primitive | Purpose | Notable props |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Button` | Actions and form submission | `variant`, `size`, `loading` |
| `Input` | Single-line text input | `invalid`, native input props |
| `Textarea` | Multiline text input | `invalid`, `resize`, native textarea props |
| `Checkbox` | Boolean or mixed selection | `checked`, `defaultChecked`, `onCheckedChange` |
| `Switch` | Immediate on/off settings | `checked`, `defaultChecked`, `onCheckedChange` |
| `Badge` | Compact statuses and labels | `variant` |
| `Avatar` | User or entity images | `src`, `alt`, `fallback`, `size` |
| `Card` | Grouped content container | Native `div` props |
| `Dialog` | Focus-managed modal content | `open`, `defaultOpen`, `onOpenChange` |
| `Tabs` | Switch between related panels | `value`, `defaultValue`, `onValueChange` |
| `Tooltip` | Supplemental labels and hints | `content`, `side`, `delay` |
| `Spinner` | Indeterminate loading state | `label`, `size` |

Every primitive accepts `className` and `style`, and forwards its ref to the root element. Components based on native elements also accept their corresponding native attributes.

## Examples

### Checkbox and Switch

```tsx
import { useState } from "react";
import { Checkbox, Switch } from "paw";

export function Preferences() {
  const [updates, setUpdates] = useState(true);

  return (
    <>
      <label>
        <Checkbox defaultChecked onCheckedChange={console.log} />
        Accept the terms
      </label>

      <label>
        <Switch checked={updates} onCheckedChange={setUpdates} />
        Product updates
      </label>
    </>
  );
}
```

### Dialog

```tsx
import { Button, Dialog } from "paw";

export function DeleteDialog() {
  return (
    <Dialog>
      <Dialog.Trigger asChild>
        <Button variant="danger">Delete project</Button>
      </Dialog.Trigger>

      <Dialog.Content>
        <Dialog.Title>Delete this project?</Dialog.Title>
        <Dialog.Description>
          This action cannot be undone.
        </Dialog.Description>

        <Dialog.Close asChild>
          <Button variant="ghost">Cancel</Button>
        </Dialog.Close>
        <Button variant="danger">Delete</Button>
      </Dialog.Content>
    </Dialog>
  );
}
```

Dialogs trap focus while open, close on `Escape`, and return focus to their trigger. For controlled usage, pass `open` and `onOpenChange` to `Dialog`.

### Tabs

```tsx
import { Tabs } from "paw";

export function SettingsTabs() {
  return (
    <Tabs defaultValue="general">
      <Tabs.List aria-label="Settings">
        <Tabs.Trigger value="general">General</Tabs.Trigger>
        <Tabs.Trigger value="security">Security</Tabs.Trigger>
      </Tabs.List>

      <Tabs.Content value="general">General settings</Tabs.Content>
      <Tabs.Content value="security">Security settings</Tabs.Content>
    </Tabs>
